From: HakiOS
Subject: [PATCH 0160] sweet-fb: boot-arg sweetmetal=1 publishes Metal's discovery properties

Metal finds a GPU by reading MetalPluginName and MetalPluginClassName off the
IOAcceleratorES service, then opening /System/Library/Extensions/<name>.bundle.
The service was deliberately published without them. With sweetmetal=1 it now
carries RedwoodMetal / RedwoodMetalDevice. Default off: without the boot-arg
nothing changes, and the GL path is as before.

Proof in the log: "SWEET METAL: discovery properties published (sweetmetal)".
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
index 135c8e0..79238e9 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -752,6 +752,14 @@ AppleCLCD::start(IOService *provider)
 	IOAcceleratorES *accel = accelOn ? OSTypeAlloc(IOAcceleratorES) : NULL;
 	if (accel != NULL && accel->init()) {
 		accel->setName("sgx");
+		uint32_t metalOn = 0;
+		(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetmetal", &metalOn, sizeof(metalOn));
+		if (metalOn != 0) {
+			/* MTLRegisterDevices opens /System/Library/Extensions/<name>.bundle and asks it for this class */
+			accel->setProperty("MetalPluginName", "RedwoodMetal");
+			accel->setProperty("MetalPluginClassName", "RedwoodMetalDevice");
+			IOLog("SWEET METAL: discovery properties published (sweetmetal)\n");
+		}
 		if (accel->attach(this)) {
 			accel->registerService();
 			IOLog("SWEET FB: empty IOAcceleratorES published (no 30 s wait in CAMetalContextCreate)\n");
